  "live_records": {
    "q-93076": {
      "dom_id": "step-q93076",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Only apple and cherry trees grow in a garden. The following table shows the number of these trees.\n\n| Apple trees | Cherry trees |\n| --- | --- |\n| $271$ | $425$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest hundred, determine the approximate ratio of the number of apple trees to the total number of trees.",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's approximate the number of apple and cherry trees by rounding to the nearest hundred.\n\n- Apple trees: $271⟶300$\n\n- Cherry trees: $425⟶400$\n\nThus, the total number of trees is approximately $300+400=700.$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the number of apple trees to the total number of trees (expressed as a fraction) is approximately\n\n$$\n\\frac{300}{700}.\n$$\n\nDividing the numerator and denominator by $100$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{300÷100}{700÷100}=\\frac{3}{7}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the number of apple trees to the total number of trees is approximately $\\frac{3}{7}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
